['# Task\n"Evaluate the review text provided below to determine if the paper should be accepted (Yes) or rejected (No). In your evaluation, consider the following aspects:\n\n- The overall soundness and rigor of the research presented, including the validity of the methods and results.\n- The clarity, organization, and presentation quality of the writing, including how well the arguments are articulated.\n- The novelty and significance of the contributions to the field, including how the work compares to existing literature.\n- The strengths and weaknesses highlighted by the reviewers, and how they impact the overall assessment.\n- The relevance of any limitations mentioned in relation to the paper\'s conclusions and claims.\n- The overall rating given by the reviewers and how it aligns with the provided feedback.\n\nYour decision should reflect a thorough and balanced analysis of these factors." \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:', '# Task\n"Given the review text below, evaluate whether the paper is suitable for acceptance (Yes) or rejection (No). Take into account the reviewer\'s assessments of soundness, presentation, contributions, strengths, weaknesses, limitations, and the overall rating. Your evaluation should weigh the positive aspects against the criticisms, considering the reviewer\'s confidence in their assessment. Ensure that your conclusion accurately reflects the overall sentiment and implications of the review." \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:', '# Task\n"Evaluate the following review for a research paper and classify it as acceptable (Yes) or not acceptable (No). Consider the reviewer\'s assessments of soundness, presentation, contributions, and the final rating. Pay particular attention to the strengths and weaknesses identified by the reviewer, especially any significant concerns or praises that may impact the overall acceptance decision. Your classification should reflect the reviewer\'s overall sentiment and the balance between positive and negative feedback. If the weaknesses significantly outweigh the strengths or if major concerns are raised about the paper\'s contributions or soundness, classify as not acceptable (No). Conversely, if the strengths are compelling and the weaknesses are minor or easily addressable, classify as acceptable (Yes)." \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:', '# Task\n"Given the review text below, determine if the paper should be accepted (Yes) or rejected (No). Consider the reviewer\'s evaluations of soundness, presentation, contributions, strengths, weaknesses, limitations, and overall rating. Your assessment should weigh the positive and negative feedback, as well as the reviewer\'s confidence level. Pay special attention to the balance of strengths and weaknesses, the clarity of the contributions, and the overall impression conveyed by the reviewers." \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:']
